WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.990
- I am just getting back
from the Apple Event

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:03.620
and I had such an awesome time,

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.340
and thank you guys so
much for subscribing.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.380
I also just hit six million subscribers,

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.750
so this has been a really
awesome and a crazy week,

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.460
and I could not do it without you guys.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.490
So a huge thank you to
everybody who followed along

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.160
on this iPhone journey and
adventure this past week.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.760
And I cannot wait because the
iPhone and the Apple Watch,

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.570
it'll all be here before we know it.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.470
So now that I'm back, I've
had a little bit of time

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.350
to decompress and think about the Event.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.670
The main highlights, of
course, in case you did miss it

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.500
is they announced three new iPhones.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.290
There is the iPhone 11 which
comes in five different colors.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.860
And the iPhone Pro and the iPhone Pro Max.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.820
The iPhone Pro comes in four colors now,

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.690
a silver, a gold, and a Space Gray,

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.880
and this new color which
is a Midnight Green.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.270
And seeing the Midnight Green in person

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.780
was actually really cool,

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.950
because the color that they
showed during the keynote,

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.270
it was kind of like a muted
color, sort of washed out.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.430
But when you see it in person,

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.620
every single time that
I've moved it around

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.100
in different lighting, it
always looks different.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.190
And I really actually
like the color a lot.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.300
Although for me personally,
even though it's not Friday yet,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.540
I haven't done my pre-orders,

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:00.870
I think I'm gonna go with the silver

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.080
because I did order the
white ceramic watch,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.510
so I would like for my
phone and watch to match.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.250
The main difference
between the iPhone 11 Pro

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.640
and the regular iPhone 11 is
the cameras and the display.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.360
So the iPhone 11 has an LCD display,

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.360
whereas the iPhone Pro has a
Super Retina OLED XDR display.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.956
There was some crazy long
term that they called it.

00:01:22.956 --> 00:01:24.920
The iPhone 11 also only has two cameras.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.120
Only, it's like, okay,
it only has two cameras?

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.950
It has two cameras because
the XR still only had one,

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.960
so this is an addition and an upgrade.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.450
The iPhone Pro has three cameras.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:37.630
It has an ultra-wide telephoto
and a wide-angle lens.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.800
And the front-facing does 4K.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.940
It's also been bumped up to 12 megapixels,

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.360
so you're definitely
getting better photos.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.010
You're also able to do
slo-mo video front-facing.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.200
And I do shoot a lot of front-facing video

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.060
when I'm vlogging.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.460
So the Pro's three cameras
are the ultra-wide,

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.400
the wide, and the telephoto lens.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.800
So being able to have those three cameras

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.770
gives you a lot more
flexibility when you're filming.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.670
And it's cool because
when you are filming,

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:01.450
you'll still be able to
see the outside frame

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.260
of whatever else would
potentially be in-frame

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.310
if you switched lenses.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.160
So that's something that a lot of

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.390
these other phones don't do.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.755
They may have these multiple cameras,

00:02:08.755 --> 00:02:11.090
but they're not really using
them all at the same time.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.380
And that brings us to FiLMiC Pro.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.770
I've used this app before,
but it's kind of something

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:18.710
that really lets you take
advantage of your iPhone camera.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.100
But this new version of FiLMiC Pro,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.660
you are able to see all of
your cameras at the same time.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.340
And this is really cool,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.170
because that's something
that I've never seen before.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.490
And something that I think is gonna be fun

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.060
for vloggers and content creators,

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.400
you'll be able to film using

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.180
two of those angles at the same time.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.860
So if I want to film a
front-facing but also

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.680
a rear-facing camera at
the same time, you can.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.930
So I can't wait to try that out.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.780
I'm not sure when the
release of the new FiLMiC pro

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.020
will be out, but when it is,

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.420
I'll definitely be doing some
extensive coverage of that.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.400
The introduction of the new ultra-wide

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.260
is something that is not new,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.300
that we've seen that in
films before and it has been

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.590
something that I've been
really wanting on the iPhone.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.930
He also talked about this
new Deep Fusion photography,

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.330
which is like a computational math,

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.420
scientific, mad scientist.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.430
I don't remember his exact precise words.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.610
So it's basically using AI

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.270
to generate a more detailed photo.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.540
So that will be a software
update later this year.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.620
But I can probably sit here
and talk for the next like

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.360
five hours about everything
that they discussed.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.340
I just wanted to do a quick little recap,

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.120
and this doesn't seem
to be so quick, is it?

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.500
Being able to shoot in the
ultra-wide is gonna be so fun

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.120
for video and vlogging, and
doing landscape photography.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.170
So I cannot wait to get
my hands on this thing

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.450
and really test it out.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.630
I think the big question
for a lot of people is

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:32.350
do I need to spend the
extra money to get the Pro,

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.430
or will I be perfectly happy with the 11?

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.530
Do I need to upgrade if I have a XS?

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.040
Do I need to upgrade if I have a X?

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.770
I think really I would
just encourage you to go to

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.000
the Apple store if you are
on the fence and test it out.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.750
Do the photos look different than

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:44.900
the phone that you already have?

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.230
Is this something that is going to make

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.440
a huge difference in your life?

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.410
Is this something that you
have the extra money to spend?

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.847
If you are a content creator,
I definitely think that it is

00:03:51.847 --> 00:03:53.770
something that you should consider,

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.020
because a lot of the stuff
is investing in your future,

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:58.120
in your career, and in
your content creation.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.450
They also announced a new iPad

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.650
which I tested out at the event.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.137
And I was playing Apple Arcade on it

00:04:02.137 --> 00:04:04.570
and I'm kind of really
excited about Apple Arcade,

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.460
mostly because it is
something that you can play

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:07.560
across all platforms.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.890
You can play on your phone,
you can play on your iPad,

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.790
you can play on Apple TV,
you can play on your Mac.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:14.520
Like, it's really cool how
this is all just integrated

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.640
into the Apple ecosystem.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.440
And it's also really
cool because you can use

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.340
a controller, yes, a
freaking Xbox controller,

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.900
or a Playstation controller
on your Apple TV,

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.200
or on your Mac, or on
your phone, or your iPad.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.840
That is something that I never
thought in a million years

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.660
would ever happen, and when
they announced that at WWDC

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.640
I was like, yeah, that's cool.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.320
So Apple Arcade is 4.99 and
also, Apple TV+ is 4.99.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.260
I thought that they would announce

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.540
some sort of a bundling service,

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.000
but I feel like maybe later
on down the line they will.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.780
But both of those prices was way less

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:44.987
than I thought it was gonna be.

00:04:44.987 --> 00:04:47.600
But that also could be is
they wanna keep those costs

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.960
a little bit lower because
if you do buy an iPad

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.660
or an iPhone, you're gonna
want things to do on it.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.130
So keeping you in that ecosystem

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:55.250
and keeping those prices down,

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.040
I feel like more people
will have access to it

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.980
and be willing to spend
those extra dollars.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.080
But the good news is they said
that you will get a year free

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.580
when you buy a new iPhone
or an iPad or a Mac,

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.470
or anything like that.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.840
So that is a nice little added bonus.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.310
They also announced an
Apple Watch Series 5,

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:10.560
which I was very excited.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.920
I kinda didn't think they were going to.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.710
I'm not sure why I thought they weren't.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.410
But it doesn't matter what
I thought because they did.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.680
They announced a few
different new watch faces.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.520
They have a new titanium, and
also a brushed black titanium.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.970
They have a new ceramic which
is the one that I ordered,

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:24.960
and I can't wait.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.960
'Cause they obviously
have the cellular and GPS

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.030
